        // This is a CEILING, not a measurement. SYS_WIN_INFO tells a program
        // how big its window is right now, and that number changes underneath
        // it on every reflow; this one never does. The difference is the whole
        // reason the syscall exists, since there is no realloc (lager can take memory
        // back, but not grow a block in place), so a program cannot grow its
        // frame buffer when its window grows. It has to
        // allocate for the worst case once and render a sub-rectangle of it.
