        //
        // Why a bitmap and not a draw call? Ring-3 programs composite whole
        // frames into their own buffer and present them with ONE syscall,
        // because a multi-call draw sequence gets torn by the scheduler (see
        // SYS_PRESENT and gnista's engine.c0). A kernel-side draw_text would
        // write straight to the framebuffer and put text back outside that
